            "source": "Hacker News",
            "category": "technology",
            "title": "Show HN: Make your logo extra bright on HDR screens",
            "description": "<p>Certain logos started standing out to me on LinkedIn as brighter/whiter than everything else around them.<p>I dug in and found out this is accomplished by adding a gain-map to an existing JPEG, visible only on HDR screens like a newer MacBook Pro. LinkedIn is the only social network I've found that isn't stripping them out, but of course you serve them up on your own site.<p>I worked with Claude Code to turn it into a little browser-based utility (no registration) and hope you find it useful!</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49402521\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49402521</a></p>\n<p>Points: 12</p>\n<p># Comments: 8</p>",
